  "prefLabel": "Gal 503.17 Cooperation in Investigations and Compliance with Board Procedures and Orders",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-10-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Gal 503.17 Cooperation in Investigations and Compliance with Board Procedures and Orders.\n\n(a) A presently or formerly certified guardian ad litem shall cooperate in investigations of complaints conducted by the board, including by providing an executed answer form as required by Gal 203.02 (e) – (f) within 30 days of the date appearing on the board’s written notification or such extended period allowed under Gal 203.02 (g).\n\n(b) A presently or formerly certified guardian ad litem shall abide by orders issued by the board or its presiding officers that are applicable to the guardian ad litem, including, but not limited to, orders issued pursuant to RSA 490-C:5-b, VI – VIII.\n\n(c) A presently or formerly certified guardian ad litem shall provide the board with information requested of him or her pursuant to Gal 404.01 (b) and (c).\n\nSource. #8941, eff 9-15-07, EXPIRED: 9-15-15\n\nNew. #11075, INTERIM, eff 4-18-16, EXPIRED: 10-15-16\n\nNew. #12010, eff 10-21-16 (from Gal 503.19)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/gal500.html"
